Task: Cross-adapter parity audit - type export parity
Phase: 3 (Framework Adapter Parity)
Scope: packages/{react,vue}/src/index.ts

Second half of the parity audit, checking the published type surface rather
than the rendered markup.

Gap found: AccessibleFallbackMode reached consumers from Svelte but not React
or Vue. The cause is a difference in export style that predates this track -
Svelte uses `export type * from './types.js'`, the other two enumerate. A new
type therefore ships from one adapter automatically and from the others only if
someone remembers.

Worth noting for future tracks: that asymmetry will silently swallow the next
new type too. Not changed here, as converting React and Vue to wildcard exports
would widen their public surface beyond this track's remit.

Also forwarded the seven new core accessibility types from all three adapters,
matching the existing convenience re-exports, so consumers can type an
announcement handler without importing @heelslide/core directly.

Full suite 468 passing, tsc and oxlint clean.
